[agent] ## How I found it
[agent] All comparison work ran on the platform: I loaded both CSVs into Hopsworks feature groups (`skew_train`, `skew_serve`), then joined them on `entity_id` via Trino SQL (delta catalog) and aggregated per-feature differences across the 200 shared entities.
[agent] **Result:**
[agent] - **f1–f4**: identical between training and serving — mean *and* max absolute difference exactly `0.0`.
[agent] - **f5**: mean abs diff `7.86`, max `43.7`. The diverging feature.
[agent] **Cause** (confirmed on-platform):
[agent] - `train.f5 = ln(1 + serve.f5)` — `max|train.f5 - ln(1+serve.f5)| = 6e-7`
[agent] - equivalently `serve.f5 = exp(train.f5) - 1` — `max|serve.f5 - (exp(train.f5)-1)| = 1.7e-5`
[agent] Both residuals are at floating-point precision, so the relationship is exact. The training pipeline applies a **`log1p` transform** to f5, but the online serving path serves the **raw, untransformed** value. The model trained on a log scale (mean ~2.2, max ~3.9) is fed exponential-scale values at inference (mean ~10.1, max ~47.6).
